[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 STP (Software Test Plan) - ADAS Control Module
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
 Scope
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
1 Identification
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-001
TITLE: Test Plan Identification
STATEMENT: This document shall be identified as the Software Test Plan (STP) for the Advanced Driver Assistance System (ADAS) Control Module, version 1.0, following MIL-STD-498 and ISO 26262 testing standards.
RATIONALE: Proper test plan identification ensures configuration management and testing traceability for safety-critical automotive systems.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
2 System overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-002
TITLE: Testing Overview
STATEMENT: The ADAS Control Module testing shall encompass comprehensive verification and validation activities including unit testing, integration testing, system testing, safety testing, and field validation for automotive safety-critical applications.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive testing overview establishes the foundation for all testing activities in the automotive safety domain.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 1
3 Document overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-003
TITLE: Test Plan Structure
STATEMENT: This document shall be organized into sections covering test overview, test environment, test procedures, test data, and test reporting following MIL-STD-498 and automotive safety testing standards.
RATIONALE: Structured organization facilitates test planning and execution for safety-critical systems.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 2
 Referenced documents
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-004
TITLE: Testing References
STATEMENT: The test plan shall reference the SRS and SDD documents, ISO 26262 testing standards, automotive safety testing guidelines, and industry best practices for safety-critical software testing.
RATIONALE: Testing references ensure consistency with requirements and established automotive safety testing patterns.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
 Test overview
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
1 Test organization
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-005
TITLE: Test Organization Structure
STATEMENT: The testing organization shall include dedicated test teams for unit testing, integration testing, system testing, safety testing, and field validation with clear responsibilities and reporting structures.
RATIONALE: Organized test structure ensures comprehensive coverage and accountability for safety-critical testing.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
2 Test levels
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-006
TITLE: Unit Testing Level
STATEMENT: Unit testing shall verify individual software components and modules with 100% code coverage, including statement coverage, branch coverage, and MC/DC coverage for safety-critical functions.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive unit testing ensures component reliability and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-007
TITLE: Integration Testing Level
STATEMENT: Integration testing shall verify component interactions, interface compatibility, and system integration with focus on safety-critical interfaces and communication protocols.
RATIONALE: Integration testing ensures system reliability and safety-critical interface compatibility.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-008
TITLE: System Testing Level
STATEMENT: System testing shall verify complete system functionality, performance, and safety requirements under various operating conditions and environmental scenarios.
RATIONALE: System testing ensures complete system validation and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-009
TITLE: Safety Testing Level
STATEMENT: Safety testing shall verify fault tolerance, graceful degradation, and safety mechanisms under fault injection, stress testing, and failure scenarios.
RATIONALE: Safety testing ensures system reliability and compliance with automotive safety standards.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 3
3 Test categories
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-010
TITLE: Functional Testing
STATEMENT: Functional testing shall verify all ADAS features including lane departure warning, adaptive cruise control, forward collision warning, blind spot detection, and traffic sign recognition.
RATIONALE: Functional testing ensures all system features operate correctly and safely.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-011
TITLE: Performance Testing
STATEMENT: Performance testing shall verify real-time response times, memory usage, CPU utilization, and system throughput under various load conditions.
RATIONALE: Performance testing ensures system meets automotive timing and resource requirements.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-012
TITLE: Safety Testing
STATEMENT: Safety testing shall verify fault tolerance, error handling, graceful degradation, and safety mechanisms under various failure scenarios and environmental conditions.
RATIONALE: Safety testing ensures system reliability and compliance with automotive safety standards.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-013
TITLE: Security Testing
STATEMENT: Security testing shall verify cybersecurity controls, authentication mechanisms, data protection, and vulnerability assessment for automotive security requirements.
RATIONALE: Security testing ensures system protection against cyber threats and unauthorized access.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
 Test environment
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
1 Test environment requirements
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-014
TITLE: Hardware Test Environment
STATEMENT: The test environment shall include automotive-grade hardware platforms, sensor simulators, vehicle control simulators, and real-time testing equipment for comprehensive system validation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive hardware test environment ensures realistic testing conditions and system validation.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-015
TITLE: Software Test Environment
STATEMENT: The test environment shall include automotive development tools, simulation software, test automation frameworks, and analysis tools for comprehensive software validation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive software test environment ensures efficient testing and analysis capabilities.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-016
TITLE: Safety Test Environment
STATEMENT: The safety test environment shall include fault injection tools, stress testing equipment, environmental chambers, and safety analysis tools for comprehensive safety validation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive safety test environment ensures thorough safety validation and compliance.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 4
2 Test tools
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-017
TITLE: Test Automation Tools
STATEMENT: The testing shall use automated test tools for unit testing, integration testing, and regression testing with continuous integration and automated reporting capabilities.
RATIONALE: Test automation tools ensure efficient testing and consistent results across test cycles.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-018
TITLE: Analysis Tools
STATEMENT: The testing shall use static analysis tools, dynamic analysis tools, and coverage analysis tools for comprehensive code quality and safety assessment.
RATIONALE: Analysis tools ensure code quality and safety compliance through automated analysis.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 5
 Test procedures
[SECTION]
TITLE: 5
1 Test preparation
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-019
TITLE: Test Case Development
STATEMENT: Test cases shall be developed based on requirements analysis, risk assessment, and safety analysis with comprehensive coverage of normal, boundary, and error conditions.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive test case development ensures thorough system validation and safety compliance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-020
TITLE: Test Data Preparation
STATEMENT: Test data shall include realistic sensor data, vehicle scenarios, environmental conditions, and fault scenarios for comprehensive system validation.
RATIONALE: Realistic test data ensures thorough system validation under various operating conditions.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 5
2 Test execution
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-021
TITLE: Test Execution Process
STATEMENT: Test execution shall follow defined procedures with automated test execution, manual verification, and comprehensive logging and reporting for all test activities.
RATIONALE: Structured test execution ensures consistent results and comprehensive documentation.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-022
TITLE: Test Result Analysis
STATEMENT: Test results shall be analyzed for functional correctness, performance compliance, safety validation, and security verification with comprehensive reporting and documentation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive test result analysis ensures system quality and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 6
 Test data
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-023
TITLE: Test Data Requirements
STATEMENT: Test data shall include sensor calibration data, vehicle configuration data, environmental scenario data, and fault injection data for comprehensive system validation.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive test data ensures thorough system validation under various operating conditions.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 7
 Test reporting
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-024
TITLE: Test Report Requirements
STATEMENT: Test reports shall include test results, coverage analysis, defect reports, safety analysis, and compliance verification with comprehensive documentation and traceability.
RATIONALE: Comprehensive test reporting ensures system quality and safety compliance documentation.
[/SECTION]
[SECTION]
TITLE: 8
 Notes
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STP-025
TITLE: Testing Guidelines
STATEMENT: The testing shall follow automotive safety testing guidelines, industry best practices, and continuous improvement processes for quality assurance and safety compliance.
RATIONALE: Testing guidelines provide guidance for test teams and ensure quality and safety compliance.
[/SECTION]
